id: pm-huolbk
title: "GH-784: SDK blueprint preflight misses host-owned flag collisions and malformed long-flag tokens"
description: "Align author-time extension lint and preflight with loader enforcement. lintExtensionBlueprint and assertExtensionPreflight currently return clean reports for a blueprint whose --json declaration is rejected at activation, and neither validator rejects malformed long tokens such as verbose or -v. Add one shared host-owned flag collision rule and explicit long-token grammar so static preflight cannot approve a blueprint the runtime quarantines."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:extensions","area:sdk",author-ergonomics,contracts,github-report
created_at: "2026-07-28T04:20:05.459Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T04:20:05.459Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: lintExtensionBlueprint emits an error-severity host-owned flag collision finding for primary and alias tokens in SUBCOMMAND_GLOBAL_FLAG_CONTRACTS; assertExtensionPreflight surfaces the same failure and remediation as runtime activation; FlagDefinition.long rejects tokens outside the canonical double-dash grammar at author-time and activation boundaries; valid custom flags remain accepted; SDK types docs fixtures property tests and installed-extension acceptance tests stay aligned
parent: pm-ugqx
reporter: github-issue-784
severity: high
environment: Published @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.7.28 in a clean installed consumer
repro_steps: "Lint and preflight an extension blueprint declaring --json, verbose, or -v as FlagDefinition.long, then compare activation behavior."
expected_result: Static preflight rejects every loader-invalid host-owned or malformed long flag with the same actionable remediation.
actual_result: "Static lint/preflight report no findings for --json while activation rejects it, and malformed long tokens are accepted and stored verbatim."
component: "sdk:extension-blueprint-preflight"
customer_impact: "Extension authors can publish a blueprint after the purpose-built preflight reports success, then lose the affected command or extension surface only at activation."
